SUMMARY:"Tales from Ovid" by Ted Hughes: Read-Aloud and Discussion of an Often Banned Poet NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nThe Roman poet Ovid has been upsetting censors for more than 
 two thousand years. The emperor Augustus exiled Ovid from Rome shortly 
 after the publication of his Metamorphoses. All Ovid's works were burned by 
 Savonarola in the infamous "bonfire of the vanities" in 1497. And when 
 Shakespeare's rival Christopher Marlowe translated Ovid a century later\, 
 the translation was set on fire again in the "Bishop's Ban." Then the U.S. 
 Customs censored some of Ovid's work again in 1930.\n\nTo celebrate Banned 
 Books Week\, we'll be reading aloud and discussing "Tales from Ovid: 24 
 Passages from the Metamorphoses\," an award-winning retelling by the 
 longtime British poet laureate Ted Hughes. Come to class and hear for 
 yourself what all fuss is about!
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-17028787
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17028787
END:VEVENT
