DTSTAMP:20261010T000000Z
SUMMARY:Author Visit with Melinda Gonzalez for Latin American Heritage Month
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Saturday October 10th at 12pm for a celebration for 
 culture community and neurodiversity As Dr. Melinda Gonzalez visits and 
 reads her childrens book: Curious Mind and Dancing Feet.\n\nDr. Melinda 
 González is a Puerto Rican scholar and poet\, who was born and raised in 
 Newark\, New Jersey\, with ancestral home in the lush mountains of Moca\, 
 Puerto Rico. She is a socio-cultural anthropologist who focuses on 
 environmental anthropology/disaster studies.\n\nIn  her book Curious Mind 
 and Dancing Feet\, we meet a young Puerto Rican Muslim girl with ADHD. She 
 explains what life is like from her perspective\; vibrant\, exciting\, 
 colorful\, and sometimes overwhelming.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Green Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Storytime
UID:LibCal-10306-17704096
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17704096
END:VEVENT
