DESCRIPTION:**4:45pm** - Shabbat Sha-Blue-Jeans (families with kids 0-2nd 
 grade) in the **YAC**  \n**5:30pm** - Dinner for all families (including J
 LC age families)  \n**6:30pm** - Family Kabbalat Shabbat (for families and
  kids ages 2nd grade and older) in the **sanctuary**  \n  \nDinner in the 
 YAC  \n  \n**RSVP for Dinner:** https://shomrei.easyshul.com/events/6ab6a2
 6d1d6f8f00272d41f5  \n  \n**Shabbat Sha-Blue-Jeans**  \nJoin Rabbi Uri for
  a spirited and fun Shabbat service.  \nWear your jeans and come ready to 
 sing and dance as we welcome Shabbat together!  \nOpen to all families wit
 h kids in second grade and younger.  \n(Older siblings are welcome.)  \n  
 \n**Shabbat Dinner**   \nFamilies are invited to join for dinner\, stay af
 ter Shabbat Sha-Blue-Jeans or come for dinner before the JLC Family Servic
 e.   \nVoluntary suggested donation of $18 per family to offset costs.  \n
   \n**Family Kabbalat Shabbat**  \nThis is a highly participatory Kabbalat
  Shabbat.   \nGeared towards children (2nd- 7th grade) and their parents\,
  grandparents\, and caregivers.  \nLed by Rabbi Uri\, Sarah Kamenetsky\, a
 nd the students from our JLC (Jewish Learning Center)  \n  \n**Questions?*
 *  \nContact the Shomrei office\, (973) 746-5031  \noffice@shomrei.org\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T220621Z
LOCATION:YAC\, Sanctuary
TRANSP:OPAQUE
