SUMMARY:"All Over the World": The Geography of Rock\, Jazz and More 
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nOver two sessions\, music historian Paul Groom will chronicle 
 the stories from key locations in popular music history and highlight the 
 links between them\, how musicians adapted to new and creative developments 
 which then become new industry standards. The presentations combine music\, 
 maps\, musicians\, narratives and memories!\n\nPaul will highlight his 
 travels to Memphis\, Tenn.: Hamburg\, Germany\; Hawthorne\, Calif.\; Rio de 
 Janeiro\, Brazil\; Central Avenue in Los Angeles\; Abbey Road in London\; 
 La Caverne de la Huchette in Paris\; Clarksdale\, Miss.\; West 70th Street 
 in New York\; S. Michigan Avenue in Chicago\, Il\; W. Rampart Street in New 
 Orleans\; Tupelo\, Miss\, Grand Boulevard in Detroit\; Cleveland\; 
 Liverpool\, England\; the 9th Ward of New Orleans\, 9137 S. Figueroa in Los 
 Angeles--and more.\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Music
UID:LibCal-10306-17328375
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17328375
END:VEVENT
