DESCRIPTION:This month\, the Bloomfield College Library has a screaming li
 neup of terrifying films for Horror Movie Week!\nOn Thursday\, October 29
 th\, we will host a film screening of "The Little Shop of Horrors" (1960)
  in L14. [Film description per Kanopy: THE LITTLE SHOP OF HORRORS is the 
 insane story of lonely florist Seymour (Jonathan Haze) and his hungry\, m
 an-eating plant\, Audrey. Seymour will go to great lengths to make sure A
 udrey is fed and happy. With a cast that includes Dick Miller\, Jackie Jo
 seph\, and a young Jack Nicholson as a dental patient\, director Roger Co
 rman and screenwriter Charles Griffith gives us a cult comic horror maste
 rpiece for the ages!]\n\nHosted by: Sprague Library\n\nAdditional Informa
 tion can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12863
 892
