SUMMARY:Library Speakers Consortium - How Money Became God: Rethinking Wealth and Greed in Modern Society with Paul Vigna
DESCRIPTION:You must register here to attend:  
 https://libraryc.org/nutleypubliclibrary/219441\n\n\n\nJoin us for an 
 eye-opening conversation with veteran journalist Paul Vigna as we examine 
 his provocative book\, The Almightier: How Money Became God\, Greed Became 
 Virtue\, and Debt Became Sin\, in which he explores the question: how did 
 money go from a tool of commerce into the dominant faith of modern society? 
 \n\nIn The Almightier\, Vigna takes readers on a sweeping historical 
 journey from Renaissance Florence to today’s global financial markets\, 
 revealing how wealth accumulation evolved from a moral failing into an 
 unspoken civic virtue. He uncovers the forgotten history of money\, tracing 
 the uneasy and often accidental alliance between wealth and religion as it 
 developed from ancient city-states to today’s secular world\, where 
 religious devotion has receded and greed has stepped in to fill the void. 
 \n\nThrough engaging anecdotes\, original research\, and fresh perspectives 
 on the causes of the many challenges we face today\, Vigna makes a 
 compelling argument that money has no power apart from the power we give 
 it.\n\nWhether you are interested in economic history\, personal finance\, 
 or the hidden cultural forces shaping modern life\, this talk is sure to 
 pique your interest. \n\nRegister today to learn more about how devotion to 
 money has replaced religion as the foundation of our society.\n\nAbout the 
 Author: \n\nPaul Vigna is an author\, journalist\, editor and speaker\, 
 with a particular focus on capital markets and cryptocurrencies. He is the 
 author of Guts: The Anatomy of The Walking Dead and coauthor of The Age of 
 Cryptocurrency and The Truth Machine. For 25 years\, he was a reporter and 
 editor for Dow Jones Newswires and the Wall Street Journal\, pioneering 
 coverage of the cryptocurrency sector. He has appeared on CNN\, CNBC\, 
 MSNBC\, Fox\, and PBS.\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:Nutley Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Nutley Library":MAILTO:events@nutley.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10315-17621830
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17621830
END:VEVENT
