DTSTART:20261114T190000Z
DTEND:20261114T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T000000Z
SUMMARY:John Lennon – Life\, Legend and Legacy.
DESCRIPTION:About the program \n\nThe real beginning of The Beatles took 
 place at a summer garden fete at St. Peter's Church in Woolton\, 
 Liverpool\, on July 6\, 1957\, marking a watershed point in music history. 
 When John Lennon was 16 years old and performing with his skiffle band The 
 Quarrymen\, a common acquaintance called Ivan Vaughan\, introduced him to 
 Paul McCartney\, who was 15 years old at the time. This one-of-a-kind 
 partnership altered the course of music irrevocably\, and our presenter 
 will trace its history.\n\nAbout the Artist\n\nJohn Paul Groom\, originally 
 from Liverpool\, resided in the same city as John Lennon and George 
 Harrison\, participated in the same Sunday school as John Lennon\, and went 
 to the same high school as Paul McCartney and George Harrison. Numerous 
 cherished recollections that I will be presenting in this discourse\n\n
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Lecture
UID:LibCal-10341-17488200
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17488200
END:VEVENT
